          "question": "How much difference does it make to how breathless I get?",
          "answer": "The search did not return anything that links quitting smoking to how breathless you get, so I can't say how much difference it would make for you.\n\nThe closest passage is from *Staying active with COPD: breathing technique, pacing and the deconditioning spiral*. It says breathlessness during exercise is expected and not harmful in itself, and that exercise is usually built up gradually, a few minutes at a time, with short periods of effort alternating with rest. It describes effort at which you can speak in short phrases but not full sentences. This passage does not address smoking.\n\nYour clinician can tell you how your breathlessness is likely to change if you stop, and can suggest ways to manage it day to day.\n\nIf your breathing becomes much worse, or you cannot speak in full sentences, seek emergency care straight away.\n\nNot medical advice. This is an educational software project. It does not diagnose or treat, and it must not be used for real medical decisions.",
